          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Brown-Gersten property
            is the statement that for certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topologies"} Grothendieck topologies
            the
            = succeed "-property" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+descent"} homotopy descent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            (i.e. their
            = succeed "-property)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            satisfies a
            %a{:href => "Whitehead-generalized+cohomology#MayerVietorisSequenceInGeneralizedCohomology"} Mayer-Vietoris-type property
            in that for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covers
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of patches
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1, U_2
            their
            = succeed "-square" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            to a
            = succeed "-square." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
          %p
            This has traditionally been discussed over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#OverSchemes"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#OverSmoothmanifolds"} further below
          %h2#details Details
          %h3#OverSchemes Over schemes
          %p
            Detailed review in in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Jardine15"} Jardine 2015, §5.4
          %h3#OverSmoothmanifolds Over smooth manifolds
          %p Write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                via its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi SmthMfd
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh\big(SmthMfd, sSet)\big)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+simplicial+presheaves"} category of simplicial presheaves
                over smooth manifolds.
          %p
            Recall (e.g. from
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Psh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \,\in\, Psh(SmthMfd, sSet)
            is said to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
            or
            %em
              satisfy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+descent"} homotopy descent
            if for
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi SmthMfd
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SmthMfd
            %li
              %p
                all its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big\{ U_i \hookrightarrow X \big\}_{i \in I}
          %p
            the canonical morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            from the value of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+diagram"} simplicial diagram
            over values of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
            of the cover
          #eq:GeneralDescentProperty.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                  %munder
                    %mi holim
                    %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇉
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{F}(X)
                  \\xrightarrow{\phantom{----}}
                  \\underset{}{holim}
                  \\bigg(
                  \\underset{i \in I}{\prod}
                  \\mathcal{F}(U_i)
                  \\rightrightarrows
                  \\underset{i_1, i_2 \in I}{\prod}
                  \\mathcal{F}(U_{i_1} \cap U_{i_2})
                  \\cdots
                  \\bigg)
          %p
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+equivalence"} simplicial weak equivalence
          %p
          #BGPropertyForSmoothManifolds.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (Brown-Gersten property over smooth manifolds,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#Pavlov22"} Pavlov 2022, Thm. 1.1
              %br/
              A simplicial presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi in
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SmthMfd
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \,in\, PSh(SmthMfd, sSet)
              satisfies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+descent"} homotopy descent
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GeneralDescentProperty"} (1)
              for all open covers, as soon as it does so
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for open covers consisting of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                  of open subsets;
              %li
                %p
                  for open covers by pairwise
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint"} disjoint
                  patches (hence by
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            %p
          %p Notice here that
          %ol
            %li
              %p in the case of an open cover by pair of patches
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∪
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      X \,\simeq\, U_1 \cup U_2
                      \\,,
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-condition" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+descent"} homotopy descent
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GeneralDescentProperty"} (1)
                reduces to saying that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℱ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℱ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℱ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℱ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ∩
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\mathcal{F}(X)
                      \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                      \\mathcal{F}(U_1)
                      \\\
                      \\big\downarrow
                      \&amp;&amp;
                      \\big\downarrow
                      \\\
                      \\mathcal{F}(U_2)
                      \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                      \\mathcal{F}(U_1 \cap U_2)
                      }
              %p
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cartesian+square"} homotopy cartesian square
                (a
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            %li
              %p
                in the case of a cover by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint"} disjoint
                patches, hence
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \,\simeq\, \underset{i \in I}{\coprod} \, U_i
                = succeed "-condition" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+descent"} homotopy descent
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GeneralDescentProperty"} (1)
                reduces to saying that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathcal{F}(X)
                      \\;\;\simeq\;\;
                      \\underset{i \in I}{\prod}
                      \\mathcal{F}(U_i)
              %p
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+product"} homotopy product
              %p
                In particular, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \varnothing
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+topological+space"} empty space
                covered by itself, this means that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathcal{F}(\varnothing)
                      \\;\;\simeq\;\;
                      \\ast
              %p
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                (i.e. the simplicial presheaf which is constant on the
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton set
          %h2#in_condensed_mathematics In condensed mathematics
          %p
            A Brown–Gersten-type property holds for
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+sets"} condensed sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+sets"} profinite sets
          %p
            This property no longer holds for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} condensed ∞-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
            are now necessary. However, one can pass to the equivalent site of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+extremally+disconnected+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact extremally disconnected Hausdorff spaces
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original discussion for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
          %ul
            %li#BrownGersten73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+S.+Brown"}> Kenneth S. Brown
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Gersten"} Stephen Gersten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic K-theory as generalized sheaf cohomology
              %em Algebraic K-theory, I: Higher K-theories
              (Proc. Conf., Battelle Memorial Inst., Seattle, Wash., 1972), pp. 266-292. Lecture Notes in Math.
              %strong 341
              Springer (1973) [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0067062"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0067062
              ]
          %p Lecture notes on this case:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"}> J. F. Jardine
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Brown-Gersten and Nisnevich descent, motivic descent
              %a{:href => "https://math.sci.uwo.ca/~jardine/LocalHom/"} Lectures on Local Homotopy Theory
              [
              %a{:href => "https://www.uwo.ca/math/faculty/jardine/courses/localhom/localhom-lecture13.pdf"}> pdf
              ]
          %p
            The version for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nisnevich+topology"} Nisnevich topology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabien+Morel"}> Fabien Morel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝔸
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
                  \-homotopy theory of schemes
              %strong 90
              (1999) 45–143 [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02698831"}> doi:10.1007/BF02698831
              ]
          %p Detailed review of these two cases:
          %ul
            %li#Jardine15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
              , Section 5.4 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Local homotopy theory
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4939-2300-7"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4939-2300-7
          %p
            Generalization of these two cases to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+decomposable+topology"} completely decomposable topologies
          %ul
            %li#Voevodsky10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"}> Vladimir Voevodsky
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theory of simplicial presheaves in completely decomposable topologies
              %strong 214
              8 (2010) 1384-1398 [
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0805.4578"}> arXiv:0805.4578
              ,
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2009.11.004"} doi:10.1016/j.jpaa.2009.11.004
          %p
            Discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/numerable+open+covers"} numerable open covers
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            with application to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoids"}
              smooth
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            and their
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+via+cohesive+path+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} shape via cohesive path ∞-groupoids
          %ul
            %li#Pavlov22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Pavlov"}> Dmitri Pavlov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Numerable open covers and representability of topological stacks
              %strong 318
              (2022) 108203 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.03120"}> arXiv:2203.03120
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.topol.2022.108203"} doi:10.1016/j.topol.2022.108203
        .revisedby
